  "id": "parsimony",
  "term": "parsimony",
  "definition": "In psychological research, parsimony refers to favoring a simpler model or variable-selection approach over a more complex one when comparing competing methods. It reflects a priority for using fewer or simpler features while weighing that choice against model performance.",
  "field": "research methods",
